//img.shields.io/twitter/follow/Scrapling_dev?style=social&logo=x&link=https%3A%2F%2Fx.com%2FScrapling_dev\">\r\n34:     </a>\r\n35:     <br/>\r\n36:     <a href=\"https://pypi.org/project/scrapling/\" alt=\"Supported Python versions\">\r\n37:         <img alt=\"Supported Python versions\" src=\"https://img.shields.io/pypi/pyversions/scrapling.svg\"></a>\r\n38: </p>\r\n39: \r\n40: <p align=\"center\">\r\n41:     <a href=\"https://scrapling.readthedocs.io/en/latest/parsing/selection.html\"><strong>Selection methods</strong></a>\r\n42:     &middot;\r\n43:     <a href=\"https://scrapling.readthedocs.io/en/latest/fetching/choosing.html\"><strong>Fetchers</strong></a>\r\n44:     &middot;\r\n45:     <a href=\"https://scrapling.readthedocs.io/en/latest/spiders/architecture.html\"><strong>Spiders</strong></a>\r\n46:     &middot;\r\n47:     <a href=\"https://scrapling.readthedocs.io/en/latest/spiders/proxy-blocking.html\"><strong>Proxy Rotation</strong></a>\r\n48:     &middot;\r\n49:     <a href=\"https://scrapling.readthedocs.io/en/latest/cli/overview.html\"><strong>CLI</strong></a>\r\n50:     &middot;\r\n51:     <a href=\"https://scrapling.readthedocs.io/en/latest/ai/mcp-server.html\"><strong>MCP</strong></a>\r\n52: </p>\r\n53: \r\n54: Scrapling is an adaptive Web Scraping framework that handles everything from a single request to a full-scale crawl.\r\n55: \r\n56: Its parser learns from website changes and automatically relocates your elements when pages update. Its fetchers bypass anti-bot systems like Cloudflare Turnstile out of the box. And its spider framework lets you scale up to concurrent, multi-session crawls with pause/resume and automatic proxy rotation - all in a few lines of Python. One library, zero compromises.\r\n57: \r\n58: Blazing fast crawls with real-time stats and streaming. Built by Web Scrapers for Web Scrapers and regular users, there's something for everyone.\r\n59: \r\n60: ```python\r\n61: from scrapling.fetchers import Fetcher, AsyncFetcher, StealthyFetcher, DynamicFetcher\r\n62: StealthyFetcher.adaptive = True\r\n63: p = StealthyFetcher.fetch('https://example.com', headless=True, network_idle=True)  # Fetch website under the radar!\r\n64: products = p.css('.product', auto_save=True)                                        # Scrape data that survives website design changes!\r\n65: products = p.css('.product', adaptive=True)                                         # Later, if the website structure changes, pass `adaptive=True` to find them!\r\n66: ```\r\n67: Or scale up to full crawls\r\n68: ```python\r\n69: from scrapling.spiders import Spider, Response\r\n70: \r\n71: class MySpider(Spider):\r\n72:   name = \"demo\"\r\n73:   start_urls = [\"https://example.com/\"]\r\n74: \r\n75:   async def parse(self, response: Response):\r\n76:       for item in response.css('.product'):\r\n77:           yield {\"title\": item.css('h2::text').get()}\r\n78: \r\n79: MySpider().start()\r\n80: ```\r\n81: \r\n82: <p align=\"center\">\r\n83:     <a href=\"https://dataimpulse.com/?utm_source=scrapling&utm_medium=banner&utm_campaign=scrapling\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"display:flex; justify-content:center; padding:4px 0;\">\r\n84:         <img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/D4Vinci/Scrapling/main/images/DataImpulse.png\" alt=\"At DataImpulse, we specialize in developing custom proxy services for your business. Make requests from anywhere, collect data, and enjoy fast connections with our premium proxies.\" style=\"max-height:60px;\">\r\n85:     </a>\r\n86: </p>\r\n87: \r\n88: # Platinum Sponsors\r\n89: <table>\r\n90:   <tr>\r\n91:     <td width=\"200\">\r\n92:       <a href=\"https://proxidize.com/?utm_source=github&utm_medium=sponsorship&utm_campaign=scrapling&utm_content=d4vinci\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Clean Proxies with No Nonsense.\">\r\n93:         <img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/D4Vinci/Scrapling/main/images/proxidize.png\">\r\n94:       </a>\r\n95:     </td>\r\n96:     <td> <a href=\"https://proxi