ble Proxy with Unparalleled Performance\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/D4Vinci/Scrapling/main/images/webshare.png\"></a>\r\n194: <a href=\"https://proxiware.com/?ref=scrapling\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"Collect Any Data. At Any Scale.\"><img src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/D4Vinci/Scrapling/main/images/proxiware.png\"></a>\r\n195: \r\n196: \r\n197: <!-- /sponsors -->\r\n198: \r\n199: <i><sub>Do you want to show your ad here? Click [here](https://github.com/sponsors/D4Vinci) and choose the tier that suits you!</sub></i>\r\n200: \r\n201: ---\r\n202: \r\n203: ## Key Features\r\n204: \r\n205: ### Spiders - A Full Crawling Framework\r\n206: - 🕷️ **Scrapy-like Spider API**: Define spiders with `start_urls`, async `parse` callbacks, and `Request`/`Response` objects.\r\n207: - ⚡ **Concurrent Crawling**: Configurable concurrency limits, per-domain throttling, and download delays.\r\n208: - 🔄 **Multi-Session Support**: Unified interface for HTTP requests, and stealthy headless browsers in a single spider - route requests to different sessions by ID.\r\n209: - 💾 **Pause & Resume**: Checkpoint-based crawl persistence. Press Ctrl+C for a graceful shutdown; restart to resume from where you left off.\r\n210: - 📡 **Streaming Mode**: Stream scraped items as they arrive via `async for item in spider.stream()` with real-time stats - ideal for UI, pipelines, and long-running crawls.\r\n211: - 🛡️ **Blocked Request Detection**: Automatic detection and retry of blocked requests with customizable logic.\r\n212: - 🤖 **Robots.txt Compliance**: Optional `robots_txt_obey` flag that respects `Disallow`, `Crawl-delay`, and `Request-rate` directives with per-domain caching.\r\n213: - 🧪 **Development Mode**: Cache responses to disk on the first run and replay them on subsequent runs - iterate on your `parse()` logic without re-hitting the target servers.\r\n214: - 📦 **Built-in Export**: Export results through hooks and your own pipeline or the built-in JSON/JSONL with `result.items.to_json()` / `result.items.to_jsonl()` respectively.\r\n215: \r\n216: ### Advanced Websites Fetching with Session Support\r\n217: - **HTTP Requests**: Fast and stealthy HTTP requests with the `Fetcher` class. Can impersonate browsers' TLS fingerprint, headers, and use HTTP/3.\r\n218: - **Dynamic Loading**: Fetch dynamic websites with full browser automation through the `DynamicFetcher` class supporting Playwright's Chromium and Google's Chrome.\r\n219: - **Anti-bot Bypass**: Advanced stealth capabilities with `StealthyFetcher` and fingerprint spoofing. Can easily bypass all types of Cloudflare's Turnstile/Interstitial with automation.\r\n220: - **Session Management**: Persistent session support with `FetcherSession`, `StealthySession`, and `DynamicSession` classes for cookie and state management across requests.\r\n221: - **Proxy Rotation**: Built-in `ProxyRotator` with cyclic or custom rotation strategies across all session types, plus per-request proxy overrides.\r\n222: - **Domain & Ad Blocking**: Block requests to specific domains (and their subdomains) or enable built-in ad blocking (~3,500 known ad/tracker domains) in browser-based fetchers.\r\n223: - **DNS Leak Prevention**: Optional DNS-over-HTTPS support to route DNS queries through Cloudflare's DoH, preventing DNS leaks when using proxies.\r\n224: - **Async Support**: Complete async support across all fetchers and dedicated async session classes.\r\n225: \r\n226: ### Adaptive Scraping & AI Integration\r\n227: - 🔄 **Smart Element Tracking**: Relocate elements after website changes using intelligent similarity algorithms.\r\n228: - 🎯 **Smart Flexible Selection**: CSS selectors, XPath selectors, filter-based search, text search, regex search, and more.\r\n229: - 🔍 **Find Similar Elements**: Automatically locate elements similar to found elements.\r\n230: - 🤖 **MCP Server to be used with AI**: Built-in MCP server for AI-assisted Web Scraping and data extraction. The MCP server features powerful, custom capabilities that leverage Scrapling to extract targeted content before passing it to the AI (Claude/Cursor/etc), thereby speeding up operations and reducing costs by minimizing token usage. ([demo video](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qyFk3ZNwOxE))\r\n231: \r\n232: ### High-Performance & battle-tested Architecture\r\n233: - 🚀 **Lightning Fast**: Optimized performance outperforming most Python scraping libraries.\r\n234: - 🔋 **Memory Efficient**: Optimized data structures and lazy loading for a minimal memory footprint.\r\n235: - ⚡ **Fast JSON Serialization**: 10x faster than the standard library.\r\n236: - 🏗️ **Battle tested**: Not only does Scrapling have 92% test coverage and full type hints coverage, but it has been used daily by hundreds of Web Scrapers over the past year.\r\n237: \r\n238: ### Developer/Web Scraper Friendly Experience\r\n239: - 🎯 **Interactive Web Scraping Shell**: Optional built-in IPython shell with Scrapling integration, shortcuts, and new tools to speed up Web Scraping scripts development, like converting curl requests to Scrapling requests and viewing requests results in your browser.\r\n240: - 🚀 **Use it directly from the Terminal**: Optionally, you can use Scrapling to scrape a URL without writing a single line of code!\r\n241: - 🛠️ **Rich Navigation API**: Advanced DOM traversal with parent, sibling, and child navigation methods.\r\n242: - 🧬 **Enhanced Text Processing**: Built-in regex, cleaning methods, and optimized string operations.\r\n243: - 📝 **Auto Selector Generation**: Generate robust CSS/XPath selectors for any element.\r\n244: - 🔌 **Familiar API**: Similar to Scrapy/BeautifulSoup with the same pseudo-elements used in Scrapy/Parsel.\r\n245: - 📘 **Complete Type Coverage**: Full type hints for excellent IDE support and code completion. The entire codebase is automatically scanned with **PyRight** and **MyPy** with each change.\r\n246: - 🔋 **Ready Docker image**: With each release, a Docker image containing all browsers is automatically built and pushed.\r\n247: \r\n248: ## Getting Started\r\n249: \r\n250: Let's give you a quick glimpse of what Scrapling can do without deep diving.\r\n251: \r\n252: ### Basic Usage\r\n253: HTTP requests with session support\r\n254: ```python\r\n255: from scrapling.fetchers import Fetcher, FetcherSession\r\n256: \r\n257: with FetcherSession(impersonate='chrome') as session:  # Use latest version of Chrome's TLS fingerprint\r\n258:     page = session.get('https://quotes.toscrape.com/', stealthy_headers=True)\r\n259:     quotes = page.css('.quote .text::text').getall()\r\n260: \r\n261: # Or use one-off requests\r\n262: page = Fetcher.get('https://quotes.toscrape.com/')\r\n263: quotes = page.css('.quote .text::text').getall()\r\n264: ```\r\n265: Advanced stealth mode\r\n266: ```python\r\n267: from scrapling.fetchers import StealthyFetcher, StealthySession\r\n268: \r\n269: with StealthySession(headless=True, solve_cloudflare=True) as session:  # Keep the browser open until you finish\r\n270:     page = session.fetch('https://nopecha.com/demo/cloudflare', google_search=False)\r\n271:     data = page.css('#padded_content a').getall()\r\n272: \r\n273: # Or use one-off request style, it opens the browser for this request, then closes it after finishing\r\n274: page = StealthyFetcher.fetch('https://nopecha.com/demo/cloudflare')\r\n275: data = page.css('#padded_content a').getall()\r\n276: ```\r\n277: Full browser automation\r\n278: ```python\r\n279: from scrapling.fetchers import DynamicFetcher, DynamicSession\r\n280: \r\n281: with DynamicSession(headless=True, disable_resources=False, network_idle=True) as session:  # Keep the browser open until you finish\r\n282:     page = session.fetch('https://quotes.toscrape.com/', load_dom=False)\r\n283:     data = page.xpath('//span[@class=\"text\"]/text()').getall()  # XPath selector if you prefer it\r\n284: \r\n285: # Or use one-off request style, it opens the browser for this request, then closes it after finishing\r\n286: page = DynamicFetcher.fetch('https://quotes.toscrape.com/')\r\n287: data = page.css('.quote .text::text').getall()\r\n288: ```\r\n289: \r\n290: ### Spiders\r\n291: Build full crawlers with concurrent requests, multiple session types, and pause/resume:\r\n292: ```python\r\n293: from scrapling.spiders import Spider, Request, Response\r\n294: \r\n295: class QuotesSpider(Spider):\r\n296:     name = \"quotes\"\r\n297:     start_urls = [\"https://quotes.toscrape.com/\"]\r\n298:     concurrent_requests = 10\r\n299:     \r\n300:     async def parse(self, response: Response):\r\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
