{"step_index":51,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-23T16:54:26Z","content":"Created At: 2026-08-23T22:24:26+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-08-23T22:24:26+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/renu5/Downloads/find-skill-repo/all%20github%20repos/handy/README.md`\nTotal Lines: 525\nTotal Bytes: 24143\nShowing lines 1 to 150\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # Handy\r\n2: \r\n3: [![Discord](https://img.shields.io/badge/Discord-%235865F2.svg?style=for-the-badge&logo=discord&logoColor=white)](https://discord.com/invite/WVBeWsNXK4)\r\n4: \r\n5: **A free, open source, and extensible speech-to-text application that works completely offline.**\r\n6: \r\n7: Handy is a cross-platform desktop application that provides simple, privacy-focused speech transcription. Press a shortcut, speak, and have your words appear in any text field. This happens on your own computer without sending any information to the cloud.\r\n8: \r\n9: ## Why Handy?\r\n10: \r\n11: Handy was created to fill the gap for a truly open source, extensible speech-to-text tool. As stated on [handy.computer](https://handy.computer):\r\n12: \r\n13: - **Free**: Accessibility tooling belongs in everyone's hands, not behind a paywall\r\n14: - **Open Source**: Together we can build further. Extend Handy for yourself and contribute to something bigger\r\n15: - **Private**: Your voice stays on your computer. Get transcriptions without sending audio to the cloud\r\n16: - **Simple**: One tool, one job. Transcribe what you say and put it into a text box\r\n17: \r\n18: Handy isn't trying to be the best speech-to-text app—it's trying to be the most forkable one.\r\n19: \r\n20: ## How It Works\r\n21: \r\n22: 1. **Press** a configurable keyboard shortcut to start/stop recording (or use push-to-talk mode)\r\n23: 2. **Speak** your words while the shortcut is active\r\n24: 3. **Release** and Handy processes your speech using Whisper\r\n25: 4. **Get** your transcribed text pasted directly into whatever app you're using\r\n26: \r\n27: The process is entirely local:\r\n28: \r\n29: - Silence is filtered using VAD (Voice Activity Detection) with Silero\r\n30: - Transcription uses your choice of models:\r\n31:   - **Whisper models** (Small/Medium/Turbo/Large) with GPU acceleration when available\r\n32:   - **Parakeet V3** - CPU-optimized model with excellent performance and automatic language detection\r\n33: - Works on Windows, macOS, and Linux\r\n34: \r\n35: ## Quick Start\r\n36: \r\n37: ### Installation\r\n38: \r\n39: 1. Download the latest release from the [releases page](https://github.com/cjpais/Handy/releases) or the [website](https://handy.computer)\r\n40:    - **macOS**: Also available via [Homebrew cask](https://formulae.brew.sh/cask/handy): `brew install --cask handy`\r\n41:    - **Windows**: Also available via [winget](https://github.com/microsoft/winget-pkgs): `winget install cjpais.Handy` \\\r\n42:      **Note:** The Homebrew cask and winget package are not maintained by the Handy developers.\r\n43: 2. Install the application\r\n44: 3. Launch Handy and grant necessary system permissions (microphone, accessibility)\r\n45: 4. Configure your preferred keyboard shortcuts in Settings\r\n46: 5. Start transcribing!\r\n47: \r\n48: ### Development Setup\r\n49: \r\n50: For detailed build instructions including platform-specific requirements, see [BUILD.md](BUILD.md).\r\n51: \r\n52: ## Integrations\r\n53: \r\n54: <a href=\"https://www.raycast.com/mattiacolombomc/handy\" title=\"Install Handy Raycast Extension\"><img src=\"https://www.raycast.com/mattiacolombomc/handy/install_button@2x.png?v=1.1\" height=\"64\" style=\"height: 64px;\" alt=\"Install handy Raycast Extension\" /></a>\r\n55: \r\n56: Control Handy from [Raycast](https://www.raycast.com) — start/stop recording, browse transcript history, manage dictionary, switch models and languages.\r\n57: \r\n58: [Source](https://github.com/mattiacolombomc/raycast-handy) · by [@mattiacolombomc](https://github.com/mattiacolombomc)\r\n59: \r\n60: ## Architecture\r\n61: \r\n62: Handy is built as a Tauri application combining:\r\n63: \r\n64: - **Frontend**: React + TypeScript with Tailwind CSS for the settings UI\r\n65: - **Backend**: Rust for system integration, audio processing, and ML inference\r\n66: - **Core Libraries**:\r\n67:   - `transcribe-cpp`: Local speech recognition with Whisper-family models (GGML/GGUF)\r\n68:   - `transcribe-rs`: CPU-optimized speech recognition with Parakeet models\r\n69:   - `cpal`: Cross-platform audio I/O\r\n70:   - `vad-rs`: Voice Activity Detection\r\n71:   - `rdev`: Global keyboard shortcuts and system events\r\n72:   - `rubato`: Audio resampling\r\n73: \r\n74: ### Debug Mode\r\n75: \r\n76: Handy includes an advanced debug mode for development and troubleshooting. Access it by pressing:\r\n77: \r\n78: - **macOS**: `Cmd+Shift+D`\r\n79: - **Windows/Linux**: `Ctrl+Shift+D`\r\n80: \r\n81: ### CLI Parameters\r\n82: \r\n83: Handy supports command-line flags for controlling a running instance and customizing startup behavior. These work on all platforms (macOS, Windows, Linux).\r\n84: \r\n85: **Remote control flags** (sent to an already-running instance via the single-instance plugin):\r\n86: \r\n87: ```bash\r\n88: handy --toggle-transcription    # Toggle recording on/off\r\n89: handy --toggle-post-process     # Toggle recording with post-processing on/off\r\n90: handy --cancel                  # Cancel the current operation\r\n91: ```\r\n92: \r\n93: **Startup flags:**\r\n94: \r\n95: ```bash\r\n96: handy --start-hidden            # Start without showing the main window\r\n97: handy --no-tray                 # Start without the system tray icon\r\n98: handy --debug                   # Enable debug mode with verbose logging\r\n99: handy --help                    # Show all available flags\r\n100: ```\r\n101: \r\n102: Flags can be combined for autostart scenarios:\r\n103: \r\n104: ```bash\r\n105: handy --start-hidden --no-tray\r\n106: ```\r\n107: \r\n108: > **macOS tip:** When Handy is installed as an app bundle, invoke the binary directly:\r\n109: >\r\n110: > ```bash\r\n111: > /Applications/Handy.app/Contents/MacOS/Handy --toggle-transcription\r\n112: > ```\r\n113: \r\n114: ## Known Issues & Current Limitations\r\n115: \r\n116: This project is actively being developed and has some [known issues](https://github.com/cjpais/Handy/issues). We believe in transparency about the current state:\r\n117: \r\n118: ### Major Issues (Help Wanted)\r\n119: \r\n120: **Whisper Model Crashes:**\r\n121: \r\n122: - Whisper models crash on certain system configurations (Windows and Linux)\r\n123: - Does not affect all systems - issue is configuration-dependent\r\n124:   - If you experience crashes and are a developer, please help to fix and provide debug logs!\r\n125: \r\n126: **Wayland Support (Linux):**\r\n127: \r\n128: - Limited support for Wayland display server\r\n129: - Requires [`wtype`](https://github.com/atx/wtype) or [`dotool`](https://sr.ht/~geb/dotool/) for text input to work correctly (see [Linux Notes](#linux-notes) below for installation)\r\n130: \r\n131: ### Linux Notes\r\n132: \r\n133: **Text Input Tools:**\r\n134: \r\n135: For reliable text input on Linux, install the appropriate tool for your display server:\r\n136: \r\n137: | Display Server | Recommended Tool | Install Command                                    |\r\n138: | -------------- | ---------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\r\n139: | X11            | `xdotool`        | `sudo apt install xdotool`                         |\r\n140: | Wayland        | `wtype`          | `sudo apt install wtype`                           |\r\n141: | Both           | `dotool`         | `sudo apt install dotool` (requires `input` group) |\r\n142: \r\n143: - **X11**: Install `xdotool` for both direct typing and clipboard paste shortcuts\r\n144: - **Wayland**: Install `wtype` (preferred) or `dotool` for text input to work correctly\r\n145: - **dotool setup**: Requires adding your user to the `input` group: `sudo usermod -aG input $USER` (then log out and back in)\r\n146: \r\n147: Without these tools, Handy falls back to enigo which may have limited compatibility, especially on Wayland.\r\n148: \r\n149: **Other Notes:**\r\n150: \r\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
